{
  "id": "events-friends-wedding",
  "name": "Events — the unofficial wedding-planning committee",
  "family": "events",
  "inspiration": "notion.com/templates/category/wedding — the wedding-planner template family (budget tracker with estimated/actual/deposit columns, vendor database with contact + payment status, guest list with RSVP + meal, seating chart, registry), plus the bachelorette/honeymoon side-trip add-on that ships in most wedding template bundles. Naming mess ('(final!!)', a trailing space, an emoji mid-property) is copied from the real 37-database workspace dump.",
  "notes": "A couple's own Notion, taken over by their wedding. Three friends volunteered as an informal committee and each bolted on a database of their own (seating chart, playlist requests, bachelorette trip), so the workspace is the same vendor/budget/timeline trio a professional event agency would build — assembled by people who have never run an event, with no naming convention and no shared vocabulary. Because it is the couple's personal space, their ordinary joint household budget sits one click away from the wedding budget.\n\nDecision points exercised: 3 (three separate 'Status' vocabularies), 5 ('Cost' as number vs text), 6 (five of the six bundled targets), 7 (five date/checkbox traps), 8 (personal vs event 'Category' collision), 10 (messy naming), plus 9 incidentally (a 2-property container and a 12-property one).\n\nDeliberately NOT asserted, because a thoughtful product person could argue either way:\n- db-vendors 'Category' [Venue, Catering, Florist, Photographer, DJ, Officiant] and db-wedding-budget 'Category' [Venue, Catering, Flowers, Photography, Attire, Music, Stationery] are arguably the same concept typed twice with sloppy wording (overlap 2/6). Merging them is defensible; so is keeping them apart. Left out of expect.\n- 'Deposit Paid?' is a checkbox in both db-wedding-budget and db-bachelorette, and 'Notes' is a text property in four containers. Whether generic fields like these should fuse across a wedding budget and a friend's trip planner is a taste call, not a regression.\n- db-guests 'Email' is an email-format property and would plausibly bundle to the built-in email relation too; only the vendor one is asserted so the trap set stays the point of this fixture.\n- db-playlist deliberately carries no titles — it exercises the no-samples path on the smallest container in the set.",
  "containers": [
    {
      "id": "db-guests",
      "name": "Guest List (final!!)",
      "properties": [
        {"id": "pSide", "name": "Side", "format": "select",
         "options": ["Bride", "Groom", "Both"]},
        {"id": "pRsvp", "name": "RSVP", "format": "select",
         "options": ["No reply", "Yes", "No", "Maybe"]},
        {"id": "pRsvpBy", "name": "RSVP By", "format": "date"},
        {"id": "pSaveTheDate", "name": "Save-the-Date Sent", "format": "date"},
        {"id": "pMeal", "name": "Meal 🍽️", "format": "select",
         "options": ["Chicken", "Salmon", "Veg", "Kids"]},
        {"id": "pPlusOne", "name": "Plus One?", "format": "checkbox"},
        {"id": "pTable", "name": "Table", "format": "text"},
        {"id": "pAddress", "name": "Address", "format": "text"},
        {"id": "pEmail", "name": "Email", "format": "email"}
      ],
      "titles": [
        "Aunt Bernadette + Roy",
        "Kat Nwosu",
        "Priya Raval (+1)",
        "The Doyle family (4)",
        "Manon Lefèvre",
        "Uncle Ger — DO NOT SEAT NEAR DAD",
        "Ines & Tomás",
        "Grandma Sheila"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "db-wedding-budget",
      "name": "💍 Wedding Budget",
      "properties": [
        {"id": "pCategory", "name": "Category", "format": "select",
         "options": ["Venue", "Catering", "Flowers", "Photography", "Attire", "Music", "Stationery"]},
        {"id": "pEstimated", "name": "Estimated Cost", "format": "number"},
        {"id": "pActual", "name": "Actual Cost", "format": "number"},
        {"id": "pDepositPaid", "name": "Deposit Paid?", "format": "checkbox"},
        {"id": "pVendor", "name": "Vendor", "format": "objects"},
        {"id": "pPaymentDue", "name": "Payment Due", "format": "date"},
        {"id": "pPaymentMethod", "name": "Payment Method", "format": "select",
         "options": ["Card", "Bank transfer", "Cash", "Dad"]},
        {"id": "pPaidFull", "name": "Paid in Full?", "format": "checkbox"},
        {"id": "pContractSigned", "name": "Contract Signed?", "format": "checkbox"},
        {"id": "pPriority", "name": "Priority", "format": "select",
         "options": ["Must have", "Nice to have", "Cut it"]},
        {"id": "pWhosPaying", "name": "Who's Paying", "format": "multiSelect",
         "options": ["Us", "Her parents", "His parents"]},
        {"id": "pNotes", "name": "Notes", "format": "text"}
      ],
      "titles": [
        "The Old Rectory — venue hire",
        "Catering — 96 covers @ €74",
        "Fleur & Vine Florals — arch + 8 centrepieces",
        "Sorcha Ryan Photography — full day",
        "DJ Halcyon — 7pm to 1am",
        "Dress alterations (2nd fitting)",
        "Letterpress invites + save-the-dates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "db-household-budget",
      "name": "Joint Household Budget",
      "properties": [
        {"id": "pCategory", "name": "Category", "format": "select",
         "options": ["Rent", "Groceries", "Utilities", "Car", "Subscriptions", "Savings"]},
        {"id": "pAmount", "name": "Amount", "format": "number"},
        {"id": "pMonth", "name": "Month", "format": "date"},
        {"id": "pRecurring", "name": "Recurring?", "format": "checkbox"},
        {"id": "pAccount", "name": "Account", "format": "text"},
        {"id": "pNotes", "name": "Notes", "format": "text"}
      ],
